<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pungo Andongo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pedras Negras de Pungo Andongo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pungo Andongo is a massif of giant black rock formations in Malanje Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, which served as a royal stronghold of the kingdom of Ndongo. After the Portuguese stormed the fortress in 1671 and ended Ndongo's last independent kingship, they built a presidio there that remained an important outpost of Portuguese Angola. The rocks, known as the Pedras Negras, are now a well-known landmark.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pungo-andongo.jpg" alt="Pungo Andongo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paulo César Santos · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_Stones_Pungo_Adongo.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
